@host = http://localhost:8080

### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### 0) Health: confirm server + dev keys are available
GET {{host}}/server-key

### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### 1) Cast a few sample votes (server encrypts one-hot u16)

### Vote A (u100 → candidate 2)
POST {{host}}/vote
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": "u100",
  "name": "Alice Example",
  "address": "123 Main St",
  "age": 34,
  "candidate": 2
}

### Vote B (u101 → candidate 0)
POST {{host}}/vote
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": "u101",
  "name": "Bob Example",
  "address": "45 Side St",
  "age": 41,
  "candidate": 0
}

### Vote C (u102 → candidate 3)
POST {{host}}/vote
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": "u102",
  "name": "Carol Example",
  "address": "9 Elm Rd",
  "age": 29,
  "candidate": 3
}

### Inspect blocks
GET {{host}}/blocks

### Encrypted ballots feed for the verifier (for your CLI fold step)
GET {{host}}/user-votes

### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### 2) MPC session — start from uploaded per-candidate tally ciphertexts
### Paste the Base64 ciphertexts from u16_tally_ciphertexts.json (CLI fold output).
POST {{host}}/mpc/sessions/start
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "source": "upload",
  "candidates": 4,
  "ctsB64": [

  ]
}

### Capture the session id
@sid = {{last_response.body.$.session.id}}

GET {{host}}/mpc/sessions/ed97a231dd1149d7b9bcd49dd707ae04/artifacts

### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### 3) DEV-ONLY masking (server generates/applies masks; insecure IRL)
### Participant A
POST {{host}}/mpc/sessions/ed97a231dd1149d7b9bcd49dd707ae04/mask:server
Content-Type: application/json

{ "who": "A", "seed": 1234 }

### Participant B
POST {{host}}/mpc/sessions/ed97a231dd1149d7b9bcd49dd707ae04/mask:server
Content-Type: application/json

{ "who": "B", "seed": 5678 }


### Quick peek (tiny session object; big arrays are on disk)
GET {{host}}/mpc/sessions/ed97a231dd1149d7b9bcd49dd707ae04/artifacts

### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### 4) DEV-ONLY decrypt of masked totals
### No body needed — server auto-loads public/u16_client_key.bin for dev.
POST {{host}}/mpc/sessions/ed97a231dd1149d7b9bcd49dd707ae04/decrypt
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Inspect masked plaintext totals (artifact list)
GET {{host}}/mpc/sessions/ed97a231dd1149d7b9bcd49dd707ae04
###
GET {{host}}/mpc/sessions/ed97a231dd1149d7b9bcd49dd707ae04/artifacts

### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### 5) Reveal masks → compute final totals
### ACTION: open verifier/sessions/<sid>/masks_A.json and masks_B.json,
###         paste their arrays below (order matters).

### Reveal A
POST {{host}}/mpc/sessions/ed97a231dd1149d7b9bcd49dd707ae04/reveal
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "who": "A",
  "masks": [
    5266,
    45138,
    60719,
    64911
  ]
}

### Reveal B
POST {{host}}/mpc/sessions/ed97a231dd1149d7b9bcd49dd707ae04/reveal
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "who": "B",
  "masks": [
    20451,
    49474,
    4785,
    44880
  ]
}

### Final transcript + artifacts (totals.json will be listed)
GET {{host}}/mpc/sessions/ed97a231dd1149d7b9bcd49dd707ae04
###
GET {{host}}/mpc/sessions/ed97a231dd1149d7b9bcd49dd707ae04/artifacts

### Optional: download everything as a zip
GET {{host}}/mpc/sessions/ed97a231dd1149d7b9bcd49dd707ae04/zip
